<title>SWITZERLAND: ABB Q1 power gen earnings higher.</title>
<headline>ABB Q1 power gen earnings higher.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Electrical engineering group ABB Asea Brown Boveri AG said operating earnings in the first quarter of 1997 had improved at its Power Generation, Financial Services, Power Transmission and Distribution segments and also at its transportation activities.</p>
<p>Earnings in the Industrial and Building Systems segment, however, &quot;were somewhat below last year,&quot; ABB said in a statement.</p>
<p>ABB does not provide quarterly results for its segments.</p>
<p>ABB's group operating earnings rose 11 percent to $472 million in the first quarter. Expressed in local currencies the earnings rise was 17 percent.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
